    <summary>Undo what a coding agent did to your working tree</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
ctrlz is a local shadow store for your working tree. It snapshots a repository
before each agent turn and `ctrlz undo` puts the tree back exactly as it was:
tracked files, untracked files, ignored-but-real files, everything git does not
cover.

`ctrlz guard` also watches directories you name and keeps a shadow index of
them, so a deletion outside a repository, or between two turns, is recoverable
too.

There is no network and no account. The per-project store needs no daemon; the
optional guard runs one only when you start it.

Commands: `ctrlz init`, `ctrlz mark`, `ctrlz list`, `ctrlz show`, `ctrlz diff`,
`ctrlz undo`, `ctrlz back`, `ctrlz prune`, `ctrlz watch`, `ctrlz doctor`,
`ctrlz guard`, `ctrlz flags`, `ctrlz recover`.

This package installs the prebuilt Windows x64 executable; it does not require
elevation or run any interactive prompt.
]]></description>
    <tags>ctrlz agent undo snapshot filesystem</tags>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
